<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Guillaume de Dole</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">13th century</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the song is set into the romance</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Le roman de la violette (Gerbert de Montreuil)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the song is set into the romance</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Divine Comedy, Paradiso XX:73–75 (Dante Alighieri)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">possibly inspired the image of the lark (disputed)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Cantos, Canto 6 (Ezra Pound)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation of parts of the song</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Cantos, Canto 117 (Ezra Pound)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">returns to the song's image</span></li></ul></section>
